<title>USA: Md. Gov promises funds for airport terminal - paper.</title>
<headline>Md. Gov promises funds for airport terminal - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maryland Gov. Parris Glendening promised $643,000 of state funds to build a passenger terminal at the St. Mary's County Airport, the Washington Post reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Improvements for the small airport, which is used primarily by private light aircraft owners, are designed to make it suitable for commuter flights from international airports in the region.</p>
<p>The U.S. Navy is also expanding operations in the area, and the new terminal would be used to handle expected increased traffic from the moves.</p>
<p>The terminal is scheduled to be completed by late 1998, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
